            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0714" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.119/705</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-06T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1918, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>677. My telegram No. 676, January 6, 2 p.m. Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    informed me this afternoon that one of the <pb facs="0715" n="603"
                        xml:id="pg603"/> objects of Nieto’s proposed visit to the United States is
                    in connection with the pending conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
